## Why This Is Asked
Gauges candidate ability to architect a small, realistic feature with performance thoughts and React hooks.

## Key Concepts
- In-memory indexing for fast, offline search
- Debounce input and memoize results
- Component memoization to avoid re-renders

## Code Example
```javascript
const EMOJIS = [
  {char:'😀', name:'grinning'},
  {char:'🎉', name:'party'},
  {char:'🚀', name:'rocket'}
];

function useEmojiSearch(query){
  const [q, setQ] = React.useState(query);
  const [debounced, setDebounced] = React.useState(query);
  React.useEffect(() => {
    const t = setTimeout(() => setDebounced(q), 150);
    return () => clearTimeout(t);
  }, [q]);
  const results = React.useMemo(
    () => EMOJIS.filter(e => e.name.toLowerCase().includes(debounced.toLowerCase())),
    [debounced]
  );
  return { query: q, setQuery: setQ, results };
}
```

```javascript
function EmojiPicker(){
  const { query, setQuery, results } = useEmojiSearch('');
  return (
    <>
      <TextInput value={query} onChangeText={setQuery} placeholder="Search emoji" />
      <FlatList
        data={results}
        horizontal
        keyExtractor={e => e.name}
        renderItem={({ item }) => (
          <Text accessibilityLabel={item.name}>{item.char}</Text>
        )}
      />
    </>
  );
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle a much larger emoji set or theme switching?
- How would you test the debounce timing and memoization behavior?

## Why This Is Asked
Gauges a beginner's ability to bridge native and JS, manage lifecycle, and design a simple stream.

## Key Concepts
- React Native native modules and EventEmitter
- useEffect cleanup and AppState handling
- Minimal backpressure and memory safety trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: JS side
function useHeartbeatStream() {
  const [beatTs, setBeatTs] = React.useState(null);
  React.useEffect(() => {
    const sub = HeartbeatBridge.addListener('beat', (ts) => setBeatTs(ts));
    HeartbeatBridge.startHeartbeat({ intervalMs: 500 });
    return () => { sub.remove(); HeartbeatBridge.stopHeartbeat(); };
  }, []);
  return beatTs;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for device sleep states and app backgrounding?
- How would you test smoothness/burstiness of beats on low-end devices?

